# Caches the interpreter and the linter drop here when these modules are run or
# checked from this directory. The repo root already ignores *.pyc; these are the
# directories themselves, so nothing a future tool writes inside them can show up as
# untracked. Without the .ruff_cache entry the only thing hiding that tree is an
# ignore file ruff writes inside its own cache, which is not something to rely on.
__pycache__/
.ruff_cache/
